# The Paladin's first job node, and three GMS effects folded into one number.
# GMS hangs an echo on a party member who then mirrors the Paladin's attacks,
# and pays three separate shares of final damage for it: 75% to the Paladin,
# 40% more output through the echo, and 15% again while Divine Blessing is on
# whoever is carrying it. Final damage sources multiply here as they do there,
# so 1.75 x 1.40 x 1.15 is one buff of 181.75% and says the same thing.
#
# The blessing's share is folded in unconditionally because this game's Divine
# Blessing already is: it ships as a permanent passive with no cast to aim, so
# there is no moment at which the echo is standing without it.
#
# The step is 2.5 points a level rather than the 2.474 an exact ladder between
# GMS's ends would want. Master is GMS's to the hundredth; level 1 lands 0.75
# under.
#
# The echo itself is worth 100% Buff Duration to one other member, granted for
# good rather than on this skill's clock -- a 30-second buff behind a 60-second
# wait cannot lengthen somebody else's buffs for only half of it, there being
# one duration per fight. GMS's 50-65% plus 1% per 1000 STR, capped at 100%, is
# rounded up to the cap it is reaching for.
#
# Dropped: everything GMS spends its description on -- picking the member by
# number key, losing the echo when they walk out of range, and the bar on
# echoing a Paladin who is already echoing somebody.
name: "Divine Echo"
description:
  "Grants an echo of your battle prowess that mirrors your attack skills "
  "alongside you. Increases your Final Damage, and one party member's Buff "
  "Duration."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_PALADIN_V skill_order: 1 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 60.0
ally_base { buff_duration_pct: 1.00 }
ally_grant_reaches_one: true
buff {
  duration_seconds: 15.5
  duration_seconds_per_level: 0.5
  base { final_dmg_pct: 1.0925 }
  per_level { final_dmg_pct: 0.025 }
}
